    "collapsible_row_list_r7Akeg": {
      "type": "collapsible-row-list",
      "blocks": {
        "item_KqpQjH": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "expand_by_default": false,
            "icon": "none",
            "title": "What is a Yizkor candle?",
            "text": "<p>A Yizkor candle is a memorial candle lit in honor of loved ones who have passed during the Yizkor memorial prayer service. It is typically a long-burning candle designed to remain lit through the full day of the observance. The practice parallels lighting a Yahrzeit candle but is specifically tied to the four annual Yizkor services rather than the anniversary date of a person's passing.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_jpw3WN": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "expand_by_default": false,
            "icon": "none",
            "title": "What is the difference between a Yizkor candle and a Yahrzeit candle?",
            "text": "<p>The candle itself is often the same format: a long-burning, glass-contained memorial candle. The difference is the occasion. A Yahrzeit candle is lit on the Hebrew calendar anniversary of someone's passing. A Yizkor candle is lit for the Yizkor memorial prayer, which occurs four specific times per year on Jewish holidays. Many families light a memorial candle for both occasions throughout the year.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_t8PETb": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "expand_by_default": false,
            "icon": "none",
            "title": "When do I light a Yizkor candle?",
            "text": "<p>The traditional practice is to light the candle just before sundown at the start of the holiday on which Yizkor is observed. For Yom Kippur, this is before the fast begins. For Passover, Shavuot, and Shemini Atzeret, it is before sundown on the first day of the holiday.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_WRTDdG": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "expand_by_default": false,
            "icon": "none",
            "title": "How long should a Yizkor candle burn?",
            "text": "<p>A Yizkor candle is generally expected to burn through the full day of observance, which means approximately 24 to 26 hours. This is why long-burning memorial candles in glass containers are the standard choice for this occasion. Our Yizkor candles match the expected duration without needing to be replaced.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_qCTeRH": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "expand_by_default": false,
            "icon": "none",
            "title": "How many Yizkor candles do I need?",
            "text": "<p>Most people light one candle for each loved one they are remembering during the Yizkor service. Some families light a single candle to honor all those being remembered together. Because Yizkor occurs four times a year, a multipack covering all four observances is a practical option if you want to keep the supply simple.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_wQeaQg": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "expand_by_default": false,
            "icon": "none",
            "title": "Can I use the same type of candle for Yizkor and Yahrzeit?",
            "text": "<p>Yes. The same long-burning memorial candle in a glass container is appropriate for both Yizkor services and Yahrzeit observances. The format serves the same practical need as a candle that burns steadily for about 24 hours in a stable, contained setup.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_xBR9WW": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "expand_by_default": false,
            "icon": "none",
            "title": "Do you sell Yizkor candles in bulk for synagogues?",
            "text": "<p>Yes. Synagogues often order Yizkor candles in bulk ahead of Yom Kippur and other observances for distribution to congregants. Bulk and wholesale pricing is available. Reach out through the contact page with your quantity and timing, and we'll work out the right approach for your organization.</p>"
          }
        },
        "item_7h3L6T": {
          "type": "item",
          "settings": {
            "expand_by_default": false,
            "icon": "none",
            "title": "Are Yizkor candles scented or unscented?",
            "text": "<p>Yizkor candles are unscented. This is consistent with the standard for Jewish memorial candles, where fragrance is not part of the observance and would be out of place in a synagogue or home memorial setting.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
